{
  "dom_id": "step-661404",
  "name": "Vectors in Opposite Directions",
  "problem": "We can still find a position vector by tracing a path from the origin to the point and adding the vectors along that path.\n\nHowever, if one part of the path points in the opposite direction to a known vector, then we write it as a **negative** multiple of that vector.\n\nFor example, consider the picture below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/d5366a68ed98e7f614ff998f69098613ea8e12d05bc27274ea66e8ce5a908cb7.png)\n\nWe are given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/80eb0b356da6e6a2315ea1466d34b914c6cad5e59ff07c4d061ea82b69ed9838.svg) and we are asked to find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/44db815dcaf0a9d405026460a655495e055df7e55a785f542f8920ca90af5418.svg)\n\nTo find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/4a2f3891f0b4c8b852767d556e1607028035219b70ab83b4910e95159a930b9c.svg) we want to match the expression\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/52599a11cea864ea801b87d8ec0ea288252afa4265395d9fbb4a4dc2815e9e7e.svg)\n\nLet ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/7502527c010624a805906c12d7a6e94363988e41b1c40771a4cc4fc82900e083.svg) be the origin, and let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/527e0abeb684dd24d8c92e45425542080c4c9493b9460bb89753fef3226c1f92.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/a14e933631f2b075c5a0bb4ab14fad2ca2790c3be2122b1fe8f4b7193fb505b2.svg) end at points ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/2109f0ae1a3679002930f1bf8bfa3490cf23c540ae6bbd50c093e5064327ab15.svg) as shown in the diagram below.\n\nSince one term in the vector sum is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/bdd7762354dbbdecb02ccf8284e0830f5421588bbb7fbf1bd9c3a9268a750649.svg) we first draw the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/cbbad9d9d0e183ac112cfdf946b99fd00718e0c6856d1a75564925b0e2760e85.svg) from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/278f99df1e14fe0ebfb61bdb72262a62670dcaa60d322148bc3ee591b278ec2d.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/bc976b12b4610c69953545d95662bf5535ef2a92eb9d9cbd63e087c85f3b98e7.png)\n\nLet ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/1aaddf0d4be4d873ff6c0600b0b239e0565a05ca8daaff7ca92bd5c70bebcf03.svg) be the endpoint of the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/a2b2f82b89941e4065ecf4c3bf612ab3d7e66fdb16c848dd2ce169480714e7ae.svg) Then\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/3a9a2959c3a256cb2651e0f00b0d7fe774f95aeee92289284bffb4c3b11b843a.svg)\n\nFrom the construction, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/f1e5980924989b13362a77d776ecbd4b7567f99e30fe26eb57ee99d18fa1d464.svg)\n\nAlso, the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/5f1f2cecb3a462fc45e60ec717c2fde5b1aaba79448a58aae1a9d3023b21b7bb.svg) has length ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/f551620762fb84e33026129595b42ef514082cc2e137b6762d75fd574d56383c.svg) but points in the opposite direction to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/853e57b0bf9a8f7c16e59d37575ae23ac4028ed66b30720af9d7d49ab595c91b.svg) Therefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/4fdd6b0f88ff6e5ea11ace72a5b61c24fe8cf6b1d85b4bceee599dde18471b5d.svg)\n\nSubstituting these into the expression for ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/3cce8321317b15087f61b778b47963fdff160e7df1e3ade0d33b040e10125994.svg) we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/71d018c5f48d3afb47781ddff61419623e8c6d15856151398905494498254880.svg)\n\nConsequently,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/57897701facaf26cf0826a2b6a12f408ae1acd8a5f4e78575a4457f66a156d9b.svg)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/e6090f180976846ce7a2e6e8d696a0fa078a471c950de6188908528c881839fb.svg) the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/792ff38b4658d1d4bbfbc57cbe93be95dd8d90b24559f601250eaa81becf8d24.svg) we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/99914dd947bc5c5acbb4d9aa989efb9fef4dc78b0242629ea0508a81e7058f61.svg)",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-661404\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"661404\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"15990\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-661404\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-8\">Vectors in Opposite Directions</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"661404\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <p>We can still find a position vector by tracing a path from the origin to the point and adding the vectors along that path.</p>\n<p>However, if one part of the path points in the opposite direction to a known vector, then we write it as a <strong>negative</strong> multiple of that vector.</p>\n<p>For example, consider the picture below. </p>\n<div id=\"graphic-39a6b33fedc1ce12d1158af1ae96aa23\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/39a6b33fedc1ce12d1158af1ae96aa23\"></div>\n\n<p>We are given that <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.1ex\" height=\"1.756ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 5348 776\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D41C\" d=\"M447 131H458Q478 131 478 117Q478 112 471 95T439 51T377 9Q330 -6 286 -6Q196 -6 135 35Q39 96 39 222Q39 324 101 384Q169 453 286 453Q359 453 411 431T464 353Q464 319 445 302T395 284Q360 284 343 305T325 353Q325 380 338 396H333Q317 398 295 398H292Q280 398 271 397T245 390T218 373T197 338T183 283Q182 275 182 231Q182 199 184 180T193 132T220 85T270 57Q289 50 317 50H326Q385 50 414 115Q419 127 423 129T447 131Z\"></path></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(788.8,0)\"><path data-c=\"3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1844.6,0)\"><path data-c=\"1D706\" d=\"M166 673Q166 685 183 694H202Q292 691 316 644Q322 629 373 486T474 207T524 67Q531 47 537 34T546 15T551 6T555 2T556 -2T550 -11H482Q457 3 450 18T399 152L354 277L340 262Q327 246 293 207T236 141Q211 112 174 69Q123 9 111 -1T83 -12Q47 -12 47 20Q47 37 61 52T199 187Q229 216 266 252T321 306L338 322Q338 323 288 462T234 612Q214 657 183 657Q166 657 166 673Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2427.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D41A\" d=\"M64 349Q64 399 107 426T255 453Q346 453 402 423T473 341Q478 327 478 310T479 196V77Q493 63 529 62Q549 62 553 57T558 31Q558 9 552 5T514 0H497H481Q375 0 367 56L356 46Q300 -6 210 -6Q130 -6 81 30T32 121Q32 188 111 226T332 272H350V292Q350 313 348 327T337 361T306 391T248 402T194 399H189Q204 376 204 354Q204 327 187 306T134 284Q97 284 81 305T64 349ZM164 121Q164 89 186 67T238 45Q274 45 307 63T346 108L350 117V226H347Q248 218 206 189T164 121Z\"></path></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3208.8,0)\"><path data-c=\"2B\" d=\"M56 237T56 250T70 270H369V420L370 570Q380 583 389 583Q402 583 409 568V270H707Q722 262 722 250T707 230H409V-68Q401 -82 391 -82H389H387Q375 -82 369 -68V230H70Q56 237 56 250Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4209,0)\"><path data-c=\"32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4709,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D41B\" d=\"M32 686L123 690Q214 694 215 694H221V409Q289 450 378 450Q479 450 539 387T600 221Q600 122 535 58T358 -6H355Q272 -6 203 53L160 1L129 0H98V301Q98 362 98 435T99 525Q99 591 97 604T83 620Q69 624 42 624H29V686H32ZM227 105L232 99Q237 93 242 87T258 73T280 59T306 49T339 45Q380 45 411 66T451 131Q457 160 457 230Q457 264 456 284T448 329T430 367T396 389T343 398Q282 398 235 355L227 348V105Z\"></path></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and we are asked to find <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.027ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.948ex\" height=\"1.597ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 861 706\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D706\" d=\"M166 673Q166 685 183 694H202Q292 691 316 644Q322 629 373 486T474 207T524 67Q531 47 537 34T546 15T551 6T555 2T556 -2T550 -11H482Q457 3 450 18T399 152L354 277L340 262Q327 246 293 207T236 141Q211 112 174 69Q123 9 111 -1T83 -12Q47 -12 47 20Q47 37 61 52T199 187Q229 216 266 252T321 306L338 322Q338 323 288 462T234 612Q214 657 183 657Q166 657 166 673Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(583,0)\"><path data-c=\"2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>To find <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.948ex\" height=\"2.009ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 861 888\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D706\" d=\"M166 673Q166 685 183 694H202Q292 691 316 644Q322 629 373 486T474 207T524 67Q531 47 537 34T546 15T551 6T555 2T556 -2T550 -11H482Q457 3 450 18T399 152L354 277L340 262Q327 246 293 207T236 141Q211 112 174 69Q123 9 111 -1T83 -12Q47 -12 47 20Q47 37 61 52T199 187Q229 216 266 252T321 306L338 322Q338 323 288 462T234 612Q214 657 183 657Q166 657 166 673Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(583,0)\"><path data-c=\"2C\" d=\"M78 35T78 60T94 103T137 121Q165 121 187 96T210 8Q210 -27 201 -60T180 -117T154 -158T130 -185T117 -194Q113 -194 104 -185T95 -172Q95 -168 106 -156T131 -126T157 -76T173 -3V9L172 8Q170 7 167 6T161 3T152 1T140 0Q113 0 96 17Z\"></path></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> we want to match the expression\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" display=\"true\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.729ex\" height=\"1.756ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 5626 776\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D41C\" d=\"M447 131H458Q478 131 478 117Q478 112 471 95T439 51T377 9Q330 -6 286 -6Q196 -6 135 35Q39 96 39 222Q39 324 101 384Q169 453 286 453Q359 453 411 431T464 353Q464 319 445 302T395 284Q360 284 343 305T325 353Q325 380 338 396H333Q317 398 295 398H292Q280 398 271 397T245 390T218 373T197 338T183 283Q182 275 182 231Q182 199 184 180T193 132T220 85T270 57Q289 50 317 50H326Q385 50 414 115Q419 127 423 129T447 131Z\"></path></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(788.8,0)\"><path data-c=\"3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1844.6,0)\"><path data-c=\"1D706\" d=\"M166 673Q166 685 183 694H202Q292 691 316 644Q322 629 373 486T474 207T524 67Q531 47 537 34T546 15T551 6T555 2T556 -2T550 -11H482Q457 3 450 18T399 152L354 277L340 262Q327 246 293 207T236 141Q211 112 174 69Q123 9 111 -1T83 -12Q47 -12 47 20Q47 37 61 52T199 187Q229 216 266 252T321 306L338 322Q338 323 288 462T234 612Q214 657 183 657Q166 657 166 673Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2427.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D41A\" d=\"M64 349Q64 399 107 426T255 453Q346 453 402 423T473 341Q478 327 478 310T479 196V77Q493 63 529 62Q549 62 553 57T558 31Q558 9 552 5T514 0H497H481Q375 0 367 56L356 46Q300 -6 210 -6Q130 -6 81 30T32 121Q32 188 111 226T332 272H350V292Q350 313 348 327T337 361T306 391T248 402T194 399H189Q204 376 204 354Q204 327 187 306T134 284Q97 284 81 305T64 349ZM164 121Q164 89 186 67T238 45Q274 45 307 63T346 108L350 117V226H347Q248 218 206 189T164 121Z\"></path></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3208.8,0)\"><path data-c=\"2B\" d=\"M56 237T56 250T70 270H369V420L370 570Q380 583 389 583Q402 583 409 568V270H707Q722 262 722 250T707 230H409V-68Q401 -82 391 -82H389H387Q375 -82 369 -68V230H70Q56 237 56 250Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4209,0)\"><path data-c=\"32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\"></path></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4709,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path data-c=\"1D41B\" d=\"M32 686L123 690Q214 694 215 694H221V409Q289 450 378 450Q479 450 539 387T600 221Q600 122 535 58T358 -6H355Q272 -6 203 53L160 1L129 0H98V301Q98 362 98 435T99 525Q99 591 97 604T83 620Q69 624 42 624H29V686H32ZM227 105L232 99Q237 93 242 87T258 73T280 59T